('73e18fa5-d0fd-5e8c-bd08-59b0d002575b'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"A tree planted on level ground is supported by cords of equal length and is perpendicular to the ground as shown in this figure. The cords are tied to the tree 3 feet above the ground and are staked at points C and Z, which are equidistant from the tree. Which statement explains how you can prove ∠C ≅ ∠Z?\n[Figure: tree perpendicular to ground; cords from point on tree (A left, X right) to stakes C and Z; B and Y at base.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"∠C ≅ ∠Z by the AA theorem."},{"key":"B","text":"△ABC ≅ △XYZ by the AAS theorem, and ∠C ≅ ∠Z because corresponding parts of congruent triangles are congruent."},{"key":"C","text":"∠C ≅ ∠Z by the ASA theorem."},{"key":"D","text":"△ABC ≅ △XYZ by the SSS postulate, and ∠C ≅ ∠Z because corresponding parts of congruent triangles are congruent."}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"aist.md","source_sha256":"e9fd07b1d1b86aee4b6b4a657186e8b73bef5b70d0a2a4adb6ffbc2a04e45d42","source_question_id":"AI-22","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/AI-22.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for AI-22","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from aist.md (AI-22)."'::jsonb),
