('b3468506-5e48-51dd-894c-c0a2a81b1d38'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"Given: △ABC with exterior ∠4. Prove: m∠4 = m∠2 + m∠3.\n[Figure: triangle with B at top (∠2), C bottom-left (∠3), A bottom-right (∠1), exterior ∠4 at A.]\n[Proof table — Statements: 1. m∠1 + m∠2 + m∠3 = 180°; 2. m∠1 + m∠4 = 180°; 3. m∠1 + m∠4 = m∠1 + m∠2 + m∠3; 4. m∠4 = m∠2 + m∠3.]\nTo complete the proof, what is the correct order of Reasons I–IV?\nI. Substitution Property\nII. Definition of Straight Angle\nIII. Subtraction Property\nIV. The sum of the measures of the angles in a triangle is 180°."'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"IV, II, I, III"},{"key":"B","text":"IV, II, III, I"},{"key":"C","text":"II, IV, I, III"},{"key":"D","text":"II, IV, III, I"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"aist.md","source_sha256":"e9fd07b1d1b86aee4b6b4a657186e8b73bef5b70d0a2a4adb6ffbc2a04e45d42","source_question_id":"AI-28","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/AI-28.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for AI-28","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from aist.md (AI-28)."'::jsonb),
