('1e7fea48-5f02-5cd6-9d9e-5c94dcd6aa28'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The equations of the 2 graphs shown are y₁(t) = a₁ sin(b₁t) and y₂(t) = a₂ cos(b₂t), where the constants b₁ and b₂ are both positive real numbers. Which of the following statements is true of the constants a₁ and a₂?\n[Figure: y₁(t) is a sine curve of smaller amplitude; y₂(t) is a cosine curve (dashed) of larger amplitude.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"0 ≤ a₁ ≤ a₂"},{"key":"B","text":"0 < a₂ < a₁"},{"key":"C","text":"a₁ < 0 < a₂"},{"key":"D","text":"a₁ < a₂ < 0"},{"key":"E","text":"a₂ < a₁ < 0"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-17","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-17.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-17","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-17)."'::jsonb),
('7dde08b9-caeb-5620-a1c4-5f141edab444'::uuid,'est','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A function f is an odd function if and only if f(−x) = −f(x) for every value of x in the domain of f. One of the functions graphed in the standard (x, y) coordinate plane is an odd function. Which one?\n[Figures: A: even W-shaped curve symmetric about the y-axis; B: V-shaped graph (vertex below origin, symmetric about y-axis); C: curve in QI and QIII like y = 1/x; D: line through the origin with positive slope; E: cubic-like curve not through the origin.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"},{"key":"E","text":"Graph E"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-18","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"}'::jsonb,'"E"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-18)."'::jsonb),
('c1c09585-8c39-5b0e-81cc-63a52a97da1b'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"As shown in the (x, y, z) coordinate space, the cube with vertices A through H has edges that are 1 coordinate unit long. The coordinates of F are (0, 0, 0), and H is on the positive y-axis. What are the coordinates of D?\n[Figure: unit cube tilted in 3-D; F at origin, E along the x-axis, H along the y-axis, B up the z-axis; D is the top vertex above the y-axis side.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"(0, 1, 1)"},{"key":"G","text":"(0, √2, 0)"},{"key":"H","text":"(0, √2, 1)"},{"key":"J","text":"(0, √2, √3)"},{"key":"K","text":"(1, 1, 1)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-19","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-19.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-19","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-19)."'::jsonb),
('15cd25e2-d78f-5d38-ba85-41fd529497fe'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which of the following trigonometric functions has an amplitude of 2?\n(Note: The amplitude of a trigonometric function is (1/2) the nonnegative difference between the maximum and minimum values of the function.)"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"f(x) = 2 sin x"},{"key":"G","text":"f(x) = 2 tan x"},{"key":"H","text":"f(x) = sin(x/2)"},{"key":"J","text":"f(x) = cos 2x"},{"key":"K","text":"f(x) = (1/2) cos x"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-20","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-20)."'::jsonb),
('1d7ce098-9bf6-5071-bbf3-3eb409abbc6b'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"A cube consisting of 8 smaller cubes that are identical is positioned in the standard (x, y, z) coordinate system. Vertex A has coordinates (2, 0, 0), and 3 other vertices are at the origin, on the positive y-axis, and on the positive z-axis, respectively. What are the coordinates of vertex B?\n[Figure: 2×2×2 cube with one corner at the origin; A(2,0,0) on the x-axis; B is the far top vertex above the y-z plane side.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"(0, 0, 2)"},{"key":"G","text":"(0, 2, 0)"},{"key":"H","text":"(0, 2, 2)"},{"key":"J","text":"(2, 0, 2)"},{"key":"K","text":"(2, 2, 2)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-21","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-21.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-21","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-21)."'::jsonb),
('9cbe062a-ada5-5e2c-bec5-248226d48636'::uuid,'est','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The set of points created by the midpoints of all chords of length 4 centimeters in a circle of radius 8 centimeters is a:"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"point"},{"key":"G","text":"line segment"},{"key":"H","text":"line"},{"key":"J","text":"semicircle"},{"key":"K","text":"circle"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-22","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"}'::jsonb,'"K"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-22)."'::jsonb),
('b477a0be-c38f-5b7c-80bc-f5051f080627'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A formula for the volume of a right circular cone with its top removed is V = (1/3)πh(R² + r² + Rr), where R and r are radii and h is height. The number of cubic feet of wood in a tree stump can be estimated using the formula given. About how many cubic feet of wood are there in the tree stump shown?\n[Figure: frustum-shaped tree stump; top diameter 3 feet, bottom diameter 5 feet, height 1 1/2 feet.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"18"},{"key":"C","text":"19"},{"key":"D","text":"38"},{"key":"E","text":"77"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-23","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-23.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-23","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-23)."'::jsonb),
('bc318733-b53c-5b5e-8ab7-fe30e41c8065'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"What is the area, in square centimeters, of parallelogram ABCD shown?\n[Figure: parallelogram ABCD; AB = 10 cm; slant side AD = 6 cm; height 5 cm drawn from A to base DC.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"30"},{"key":"G","text":"40"},{"key":"H","text":"50"},{"key":"J","text":"55"},{"key":"K","text":"60"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-24","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-24.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-24","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-24)."'::jsonb),
('a47346a5-99a3-5be4-ba50-6000222b7c2f'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In the figure, E is a point on side AB of rectangle ABCD. The measures given are in inches. What is the area of △DEC, in square inches?\n[Figure: rectangle ABCD with A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-right, D bottom-left; E on AB with AE = 3; AB = 8; BC = 4.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"12"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"20"},{"key":"E","text":"32"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-25","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-25.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-25","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-25)."'::jsonb),
('64efafd4-3fc8-5c27-9593-f32ba383e625'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The domain of the function y(x) = 3 cos(5x − 4) + 1 is all real numbers. Which of the following is the range of the function y(x)?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"−3 ≤ y(x) ≤ 3"},{"key":"B","text":"−4 ≤ y(x) ≤ 3"},{"key":"C","text":"−4 ≤ y(x) ≤ 2"},{"key":"D","text":"−2 ≤ y(x) ≤ 4"},{"key":"E","text":"All real numbers"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-26","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-26)."'::jsonb),
('e2766210-404e-5267-9104-1a7c659f5e43'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In the figure, both solids consist of 4 cubes, each 1 unit on a side. In the solid on the right, the 4 cubes form a rectangular prism that is 2 units long, 1 unit wide, and 2 units high. The solid on the left is the result of moving Cube D from its position above Cube C to beside it so that Cubes B, C, and D form a rectangular prism 3 units long, 1 unit wide, and 1 unit high. To the nearest percent, the total surface area of the solid on the right is what percent less than the total surface area of the solid on the left?\n[Figure: left solid: 3 cubes in a row (A above B; B, C, D in a row); right solid: 2×1×2 block (A, D on top of B, C).]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"0%"},{"key":"G","text":"2%"},{"key":"H","text":"6%"},{"key":"J","text":"11%"},{"key":"K","text":"13%"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-27","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-27.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-27","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-27)."'::jsonb),
('786c7d8d-ff3a-5586-a7cd-c56a227bc214'::uuid,'est','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A parabola with vertex (3, 7) and axis of symmetry x = 3 crosses the x-axis at (3 + √21, 0). At what other point, if any, does the parabola cross the x-axis?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"(3 − √21, 0)"},{"key":"G","text":"(−3 − √21, 0)"},{"key":"H","text":"(−3 + √21, 0)"},{"key":"J","text":"No other point"},{"key":"K","text":"Cannot be determined from the given information"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-28","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-28)."'::jsonb),
('6165ca57-c185-5815-be23-fc44b53581c8'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"An angle with measure ϕ is shown in the standard (x, y) coordinate plane. The angle with measure ϕ has the positive x-axis as one side and has the portion of the line y = x shown as its other side. What is the value of sin ϕ?\n[Figure: the ray of y = x in Quadrant III; angle ϕ measured from the positive x-axis to that ray.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"−√3/2"},{"key":"G","text":"−√2/2"},{"key":"H","text":"−√3/3"},{"key":"J","text":"√2/2"},{"key":"K","text":"√3/2"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-29","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-29.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-29","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-29)."'::jsonb),
('48ad3e6f-1114-53ba-a03a-cc636770beef'::uuid,'est','"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"The amount of money, A dollars, in a savings account after t years is given by A = P + Prt, where P dollars is the amount of money in the account originally and r is the rate of simple interest. Which of the following expressions gives P in terms of A, r, and t?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"A/(1 + rt)"},{"key":"B","text":"(1 + rt)/A"},{"key":"C","text":"(A − P)/(rt)"},{"key":"D","text":"A/(2rt)"},{"key":"E","text":"A − rt"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-30","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-30)."'::jsonb),
('e4b04309-6d9a-5388-b9d4-78b8d3ae8fcd'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The height and radius of the right circular cylinder shown are given in meters. What is the volume, in cubic meters, of the cylinder?\n[Figure: cylinder with radius 5 and height 6.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"30π"},{"key":"B","text":"31π"},{"key":"C","text":"150π"},{"key":"D","text":"180π"},{"key":"E","text":"900π"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-31","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-31.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-31","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-31)."'::jsonb),
('16dc2884-4d40-5181-a7c4-5ffaf1d4c4f3'::uuid,'est','"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"If a = 2b − 10 and b = 3a − 5, then a ="'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"7"},{"key":"D","text":"−4"},{"key":"E","text":"−3"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-32","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-32)."'::jsonb),
('2bda3f80-6558-5a8f-92ba-dc30099ff624'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In Figure 1, XY ∥ WZ. What is c in terms of a and b?\n[Figure 1: quadrilateral WXYZ with XY ∥ WZ; diagonal XZ and segment WY crossing inside; angle a at Z, angle b at the intersection, angle c at Y.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"a + b"},{"key":"B","text":"a − b"},{"key":"C","text":"b − a"},{"key":"D","text":"180 − a − b"},{"key":"E","text":"180 − a + b"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-33","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/T1-33.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for T1-33","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-33)."'::jsonb),
('7937166c-c4ac-541e-823c-604d1210c931'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"What is the area of the base of a triangular pyramid with a volume of 88 cm³ and a height of 16 cm?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"5.5 cm²"},{"key":"B","text":"11 cm²"},{"key":"C","text":"8 cm²"},{"key":"D","text":"16.5 cm²"},{"key":"E","text":"22 cm²"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-34","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-34)."'::jsonb),
('69b64b75-c0c7-5140-be71-298771bfcfe2'::uuid,'est','"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"√(a + b)/√(a − b) ="'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"√(a² + b²)/(a − b)"},{"key":"C","text":"√(a² − b²)/(a − b)"},{"key":"D","text":"√(a − b)"},{"key":"E","text":"−1"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-35","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-35)."'::jsonb),
('515db793-e679-514b-bbed-c923dbdd82a2'::uuid,'est','"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The cost of 2 candy bars and 4 sodas is $6.00. If the cost of 3 sodas is $3.30, then what is the cost of 1 candy bar?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"$1.10"},{"key":"B","text":"$2.70"},{"key":"C","text":"$1.35"},{"key":"D","text":"$0.80"},{"key":"E","text":"$1.60"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t1.md","source_sha256":"eef682d7d604550f5b03d4515fc8ad2b38118fd3a6267cd26237107865237ce6","source_question_id":"T1-36","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t1.md (T1-36)."'::jsonb),
